abstract: >
The FatherTimeSDKP framework is a deterministic unified theoretical
physics model comprising: SDKP (Size x Density x Kinetics x
Position), SD&N (Shape x Dimension x Number), EOS (Earth Orbital
Speed constant v=29780 m/s), SDVR (macro tensor formalism), the
Amiyah Rose Smith Law (modified time dilation resolving the 56 us/day
Lunar Offset), QCC/QCC0 (Quantum Code of Creation, 64-qubit
simulation at 38-sigma significance), the Kapnack Solver (P vs NP
solution extended to 3/6/9 vortex harmonics), LLAL (Loop-Learning
Adaptive Logic), Crystal-12 Lattice Dynamics, and the Digital Crystal
Protocol (DCP) for sovereign authorship and IP verification.

Key validated results include: GPS clock drift prediction (100%),
EOS time dilation (99.86%), M87 black hole shadow (96.8%), LIGO O3
gravitational waves (99.99%), geothermal gradient (96%), UPCF
(99.7%), and Mars relativistic clock drift of 477.14 us/day
(99.79% accuracy, predating the Ashby/Patla NIST paper by four
months, timestamped at DOI 10.5281/zenodo.18052963).

The June 2026 preprint establishes: the geometric remainder
delta_circle = 1 - 0.999… is physically real (the minimum
irreducible quantum of circular geometry); the 9-family harmonic
cascade H_n = 1/(9x10^n) with the 0.0111% law at H_3; pi
irrationality as accumulated geometric remainder; and the SDKP
master equation for macroscopic quantum superposition applied to the
2026 Nature Physics Schrodinger cat state experiment using the
corrected SD&N 24-node centered hexagonal geometry yielding phase
factor phi = pi/12.

